description:
A few weeks ago, I reported sighting what was either one (1) object glowing with many lights forming a wide V-shape - or - perhaps as many as twenty (20) bright objects glowing while forming a wide V-shape, high over the city of Oaxaca, Mexico. Cannot imagine migratory birds glowing bright at a high altitude and then blinking out. That event inspired me to keep watching the night sky when it is reasonably clear. Last night was perfectly clear.
8:00 PM: All of the moon was fully visible in an opaque way with a quarter of it shining brightly.
8:15 PM: I was looking at the northern sky where three stars form a triangle, or, pyramid-shape (when one connects the dots);
* I noted what appeared to be a tiny star which appeared to be quite close to one of the two lower stars, but noticed it was moving slowly,
the way a small plane would;
* I considered it might be a satellite until it started going downward at a 60-degree angle, as though it were landing in the mountains;
* The extreme altitude of the object, combined with the expansive and steep and thus uninhabitable mountains it was over (which define the
northern limit of Oaxaca-City) surely could not be used for drug…
